  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, welcome back! That message is expected after two weeks off. Your laptop last checked in 12 days ago, which lines up with your leave, and nothing else on it looks wrong. It just needs to reconnect so it can pick up the updates and security settings it missed. Please: 1) Turn the laptop on and connect it to the internet. 2) Sign in and leave it on and connected for about 30 minutes. 3) Restart it once. Then reply to this ticket and we'll check that it has reported in. If it still shows as not checking in after that, we'll pass it to our next-level team. Thanks!",
  "internal_note": "User: Sofia Rossi (id 7), active account, no lockouts. Device BL-LT-0107 (Win 11 Pro), assigned to her, offline. Last check-in 2026-09-27T15:10Z, warning 'No check-in for 12 days', which matches the two weeks of leave she reported. Disk is fine (54.7% free). Device isn't lost and the user isn't a former employee, so KB-021 and the KB-018 escalation conditions don't apply. Gave her the KB-018 fix steps: power on, connect, stay signed in 30 min, restart. Next step: when she replies, re-run check_device_status to confirm a new check-in. If the device is online but still not checking in after the restart, escalate to Tier 2 per KB-018.",
